@startuml sc-moves-layers
' SPEC: _spec/apps/ui/starchess/sc-moves.puml
' purpose: SC-native classical move generator — scMoves.ts, its three consumers, the BoardMoveProvider seam, and the classical boundary no StarChess concept crosses.
!include ../../../themes/proveo.puml

skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam defaultTextAlignment left

title StarChess · scMoves.ts — SC-native classical legality (layers & seam)

package "apps/ui/src/starchess — SC RULES layer" {
  component "scMoves.ts\nscMovesFrom / scMovesFor / isScMoveShape\nauthoritative SC classical legality" as SCM <<app>>
  component "board.ts\nattacksSquare + clearRay — piece geometry" as BRD <<app>>
  component "rookSiegeMode.ts\nisRookSiegedAfterB — siege truth after queued B" as SIEGE <<app>>
  component "mines.ts\nspider mines — advisory only" as MIN <<app>>
  component "vision.ts\nsieged rook 9x9 grid vs tank 5x5 rectangle" as VIS <<db>>
}

package "Consumers" {
  component "starchess/hooks/useScMoveProvider.ts\nUI adapter — implements BoardMoveProvider" as PROV <<app>>
  component "starchess/demos/adjutant.ts\nadjutant — strategy only" as BRAIN <<app>>
  component "starchess/scValidate.ts\nassertClassicalBaseline — opt-in geometry, DEFAULT OFF" as VAL <<error>>
}

package "Seam — variant-agnostic" {
  component "types/board.ts\nBoardMoveProvider\ndestinations / commit / canSelect? / suppressHoverEval?" as SEAM <<host>>
}

package "Classical boundary — NO StarChess concept crosses" {
  component "hooks/useChessBoard.ts\ntakes an OPTIONAL provider" as UCB <<app>>
  component "hooks/useMoveExecutor.ts\nchess.js gate at :164" as UME <<app>>
  component "store/gameStore.ts\naddMove -> _game.move()" as GS <<app>>
}

component "starchess/starChessStore.ts\nqueueScAction — the C action" as STORE <<async>>
cloud "chess.js\nclassical legality — NOT authoritative for StarChess" as CJS <<cloud>>

SCM ARROW_MAIN     BRD   : leap + ray geometry
SCM ARROW_OPTIONAL SIEGE : siege state after queued B
SCM ARROW_OPTIONAL MIN   : hostileMineOnTo flag
SCM ARROW_OPTIONAL VIS   : siege footprint authority

PROV  ARROW_MAIN     SCM : destinations via ""scMovesFrom""
BRAIN ARROW_MAIN     SCM : candidates via ""scMovesFor""
VAL   ARROW_OPTIONAL SCM : opt-in ""isScMoveShape"" — off by default

PROV ARROW_MAIN     SEAM : implements
UCB  ARROW_OPTIONAL SEAM : optional provider — absent by default
PROV ARROW_QUEUE    STORE : commit queues the C action

UCB ARROW_CLOUD CJS : destinations at :437 and :465
UCB ARROW_MAIN  UME : no provider — unchanged default
UME ARROW_CLOUD CJS : gate at :164
UME ARROW_MAIN  GS  : " ""addMove(...)"" "
GS  ARROW_CLOUD CJS : " ""_game.move()"" "

UCB ARROW_ERROR UME : errorLabel(bypassed entirely under a provider)

note right of SCM
  **Exports.**
  * ""scMovesFrom(map, from, color, opts?) : ScMove[]"" — every SC-legal
    classical move from one square. The UI needs this for highlights.
  * ""scMovesFor(map, color, opts?) : ScMove[]"" — the full list for a
    colour. The brain needs this.
  * ""isScMoveShape(piece, from, to) : boolean"" — shape-only geometry that
    **deliberately ignores path blockers**, so fog path-discovery intents
    stay queueable. For opt-in validation only.
  ----
  ""ScMove"" carries ""from"", ""to"", ""piece"", ""color"", ""capture"",
  ""promotes"", ""firesInPlace"", ""dropsAtResolve"", ""isPawnDoubleStep"",
  ""hostileMineOnTo"".
  ""ScMoveOptions"" carries ""siegedRooks"" — resolved **after** queued B
  toggles via ""rookSiegeMode.isRookSiegedAfterB"", **never** raw
  ""snap.siegedRooks"" — and ""mines"".
  Lives in the SC rules layer as a sibling of ""board.ts"" / ""mines.ts"",
  **not** under ""demos/"".
end note

note bottom of SEAM
  **The seam is variant-agnostic.** ""BoardMoveProvider"" =
  ""{ destinations(square), commit({from, to, requestPromotion}),""
  ""  canSelect?, suppressHoverEval? }"".
  ""useChessBoard"" takes it as an **optional** input: when it is absent
  every path is byte-identical to today's chess.js behaviour. When it is
  present the hook bypasses ""useMoveExecutor"" and ""gameStore.addMove""
  entirely, and suppresses the Stockfish hover-eval — which would throw on
  an SC-legal move that chess.js rejects.
  ""useChessBoard"", ""useMoveExecutor"" and ""gameStore"" **stay classical**:
  no SCFEN, no gas, no siege, no fog, no mines ever reach them.
end note

note bottom of CJS
  **Why chess.js stops being authoritative.** Today the clickable
  destinations come from ""g.moves({ square, verbose: true })"" at
  ""hooks/useChessBoard.ts"":437 and :465, and COMMIT passes two more
  chess.js gates — ""hooks/useMoveExecutor.ts"":164 then
  ""gameStore.addMove"" -> ""_game.move()"".
  With the **king-duel** rule two kings may legally stand adjacent
  (resolve.puml). chess.js then reports the side-to-move in check and
  collapses ""moves()"" to a single entry — measured: ""Kxd2"" only, versus
  16 when the kings are apart — and the SC resolver **drops** that plan.
  Net effect: human classical play is hard-locked.
end note

note bottom of VAL
  **The SC engine validates NO classical geometry today.**
  ""assertClassicalBaseline"" (""scValidate.ts"":43-93) checks only three
  things: a piece of the acting colour exists on ""from"", a sieged rook
  cannot relocate, and ""to"" is not an ally. Verified consequence: a knight
  queued ""b1->e5"" and a pawn queued ""b2->b4"" were both **accepted and
  executed**.
end note

