note over UCB, PROV
  **The optional-provider contract.** ""useChessBoard"" is the only place the
  two worlds meet, and it meets them through one variant-agnostic type in
  ""types/board.ts"". With no provider, every branch above is the code that
  ships today — byte-identical. With a provider, StarChess legality is
  authoritative and the three chess.js gates are all skipped.
  Nothing in ""useChessBoard"", ""useMoveExecutor"" or ""gameStore"" learns a
  StarChess concept.
end note

note over STORE
  Queue shape is unchanged: **≤1 classical per side** per turn
  (scfen-queue.puml). Resolution — including king-square plans being
  dropped, fog path reveal, and the king duel at 1 HP per checker — is
  specified in resolve.puml. Wins are HP-only (starchess-mode.puml).
end note
@enduml

@startuml sc-moves-rules
' purpose: Per-piece SC classical legality table, what is deliberately not implemented, and the open decisions gating enforcement.
!include ../../../themes/proveo.puml

skinparam defaultTextAlignment left

title StarChess · scMoves.ts — rule table (all entries verified)

note as RULES
  <size:14>**SC classical legality, per piece**</size>
  ====
  **pawn**
  * Single push to an **empty** square.
  * **Free classical double** push only from the start rank, with the mid
    square and the target both empty. Authority:
    ""starchess/hooks/useMarineDoubleStep.ts"":24-25,125-145 and
    ""starchess/specials/pawnDouble.ts"":29 ""canClassicalPawnDouble"" —
    //start-rank doubles are free classical//.
  * That is **distinct** from the 1-gas ""pawnDouble"" special, which is a
    **+1 forward** gas step (any rank) and may stack with classical same turn.
  * Diagonal capture of an **enemy** only. **No en passant.**
  * ""promotes"" is set when landing on the last rank; the caller must then
    supply ""promotion"".
  ----
  **knight, king** — leap geometry via ""board.ts"" ""attacksSquare"".
  The king has **no self-check filter** and **no castling**, and **may** step
  adjacent to the enemy king and into fire — it **duels**, at 1 HP per
  checker (resolve.puml). This is the bug being fixed: chess.js forbids it.
  ----
  **bishop, rook, queen** — ""attacksSquare"" including its ""clearRay()"", so
  blocked rays truncate: **inclusive** of a first enemy, **exclusive** of a
  first ally.
  ----
  **SIEGED rook — artillery, not a slider.**
  * Fire is **vision-shaped** over the 9x9 siege footprint — Chebyshev
    distance ≤ 4 — **not** rook lines.
  * **Captures only**, no quiet moves, emitted with ""firesInPlace: true""
    because the tank does not relocate.
  * Verified two ways: ""vision.ts"":208-217 gives a sieged rook
    ""addSquareGrid(..., 9)"" versus a tank's 5x5 rectangle; and
    ""__tests__/siegedRookScfen.test.ts"":141-165 queues a sieged rook
    ""d4->h7"" — not a rook line, Chebyshev 4 — and asserts it resolves as a
    capture of ""nh7"".
  * Unsieging costs 1 gas via the ""rookSiege"" B toggle.
  ----
  **ally on the destination** — never emitted.
  ----
  **enemy KING on the destination** — emitted, but flagged
  ""dropsAtResolve: true"". The resolver **drops** such plans
  (""resolveTurn.ts"":338-377) with no relocation and no HP chip, so the plan
  silently burns the side's one classical action. It is a **trap** the UI and
  the brain must filter out. Validation must keep **accepting** it, because
  fog path-discovery en route to a king square does occupy.
  ----
  **mines** — never restrict legality. ""hostileMineOnTo"" is **advisory only**.
  ----
  **fog** — **not** filtered inside the generator: occupancy is a **caller
  parameter**. v1 passes the full placement. A viewer-masked map — unlit
  enemy pieces treated as empty — is a follow-up decision, because filtering
  the destination **list** would leak information, and truncating rays at the
  fog edge would make fog path-discovery intents unqueueable.
end note

note as NOTIMPL
  <size:14>**Deliberately NOT implemented**</size> — state it, do not imply it
  ====
  * castling
  * en passant
  * self-check / pin filtering
  * check / checkmate / stalemate
  * queue-time path-blocker rejection
  * B / F special generation
  * gas budgeting
end note

note as OPEN
  <size:14>**Open / unresolved**</size>
  ====
  * ""assertClassicalBaseline"" geometry enforcement is **opt-in and DEFAULT
    OFF**. Turning it on later is blocked on two audits:
  ** scripted demo plies — ""demos/kingHunt.ts"" ""KING_HUNT_PLY_SC"" and its
     siblings are built through ""addScAction"" **at module load**, so a
     validator throw is a module-load crash;
  ** fog path intents in ""pathRevealPhase3.test.ts"", whose whole point is a
     **blocked ray** — hence ""isScMoveShape"" must stay shape-only.
  ----
  * **pawnDouble gas step (fixed):** +1 forward only
    (""pawnSingleTarget""); may stack with classical same turn
    (B+C or C+F). ""endScTurn"" rewrites C after B relocate and
    rides F pawnDouble on the post-C square.
  ----
  * A human-readable **SCSAN is explicitly NOT the validation mechanism**.
    SAN can only be parsed by consulting a move generator, so it is
    //downstream// of ""scMoves.ts"". SC's queue notation is already
    coordinate-based and unambiguous, and ""STARCHESS_FEN.md"":42's
    ""C=a1a8>xa5"" intent-to-resolved form expresses something SAN cannot.
  ----
  * **Cross-references:** ""scfen-queue.puml"" (queue shape, ≤1 classical per
    side), ""resolve.puml"" (king-square plans dropped; fog path reveal; king
    duel and per-checker HP), ""starchess-mode.puml"" (HP-only wins).
end note

